  "subtitle": "Ethiopian cardamom celebration bread with a carved surface pattern",
  "excerpt": "Himbasha is a slightly sweet, cardamom-spiced Ethiopian and Eritrean celebration bread baked in a wide, flat round. The dough is softer and more enriched than everyday bread, with a gentle aniseed or cardamom flavour that varies by household. Before baking, the surface is pressed with a decorative pattern using a fork or fingers (typically a wheel of radiating segments) that gives the finished bread its distinctive look.",
