  "sourceType": "CLASSIC",
  "sourceNotes": "Himbasha (also spelled himbasha or hambashe) is traditional to the Tigrinya-speaking communities of Eritrea and the Tigray region of Ethiopia, where it is made for celebrations including weddings, holidays, and welcoming guests. It is documented in Eritrean and Ethiopian food culture references and diaspora community cooking collections. The cardamom-spiced version with its carved surface pattern is the most widely known form outside East Africa.",
